    "summary": "Epic Dark Star marathon with early Main Ten jam and soaring second‑set flow",
    "blurb": "The Fillmore show delivers a monumental Dark Star > The Other One > Dark Star sequence backed by a rare early Main Ten jam. Jerry’s lead work is inspired, while the band rides high energy through Saint Stephen, The Eleven and Caution. Soundboard recordings capture the performance with excellent clarity.",
    "review": "November 8, 1969 at the Fillmore Auditorium finds the Dead in top form, launching a marathon second set that still feels fresh to listeners today. After a solid first set, the band launches into an unforgettable Dark Star > The Other One > Dark Star trek, where Jerry Garcia’s soaring leads and Phil Lesh’s propulsive bass turn the improvisation into a celestial journey. The momentum never wanes as the group weaves through Uncle John's Band Jam, Saint Stephen, The Eleven and a tightly knit Caution (Do Not Stop On Tracks), before diving into an early incarnation of The Main Ten that foreshadows later Playing In The Band explorations. The show’s energy stays high throughout, highlighted by crisp soundboard capture that lets every nuance—from Pigpen’s organ swells to Mickey and Billy’s interlocking drums—shine through.",
